msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/tools/enclose_and_fill.rst:18
msgid "|toolenclosefill|"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/tools/enclose_and_fill.rst:20
msgid ""
"The Enclose and Fill Tool is a different method of filling large colored "
"areas. Instead of :ref:`selecting each area you want to fill <fill_tool>`, "
"or :ref:`drawing the associated color of each area <colorize_mask>`, this "
"tool allows you to select an area, and it will fill everything inside said "
"area."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/tools/enclose_and_fill.rst:24
msgid ".. image:: images/tools/enclose_and_fill_basic_usage.png"
msgstr ".. image:: images/tools/enclose_and_fill_basic_usage.png"

#: ../../reference_manual/tools/enclose_and_fill.rst:24
msgid ""
"Simple usage of the enclose and fill. Draw a rectangle around everything you "
"wish to fill and :program:`Krita` will try to find all possible areas inside "
"that rectangle that can be filled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/tools/enclose_and_fill.rst:27
msgid "Tool Options"
msgstr "Voľby nástroja"

#: ../../reference_manual/tools/enclose_and_fill.rst:30
msgid "Enclosing Method"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/tools/enclose_and_fill.rst:31
msgid ""
"What kind of method to use for the enclosing area. Different images call for "
"different methods."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/tools/enclose_and_fill.rst:33
msgid "Rectangle"
msgstr "Obdĺžnik"

#: ../../reference_manual/tools/enclose_and_fill.rst:34
msgid "Use a rectangle to draw the enclosing area."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/tools/enclose_and_fill.rst:35
msgid "Ellipse"
msgstr "Elipsa"

#: ../../reference_manual/tools/enclose_and_fill.rst:36
msgid ""
"Use an ellipse, much like the elliptical selection to draw the enclosing "
"area."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/tools/enclose_and_fill.rst:37
msgid "Bezier Curve"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/tools/enclose_and_fill.rst:38
msgid "Use a bezier curve to draw the enclosing area."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/tools/enclose_and_fill.rst:39
msgid "Lasso"
msgstr "Laso"

#: ../../reference_manual/tools/enclose_and_fill.rst:40
msgid "Use a freehand selection to draw out the enclosing area."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/tools/enclose_and_fill.rst:42
msgid "Brush"
msgstr "Štetec"

#: ../../reference_manual/tools/enclose_and_fill.rst:42
msgid ""
"Use a brush with the current brush size to draw out an enclosing area. The "
"brush size is determined by the size of the active brush, and can be resized "
"with :kbd:`Shift` + |mouseleft|."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/tools/enclose_and_fill.rst:45
msgid "What to fill"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/tools/enclose_and_fill.rst:46
msgid ""
"Besides choosing how to create an enclosing area, it is also possible to "
"choose which found regions will be filled. Krita can differentiate between "
"the color (or lack thereof) of a region as well as the colors it is "
"surrounded by. For some of these options a specific color needs to be "
"selected, and thus a color selection button is shown. The :guilabel:`Region "
"Extent` options control how precise a given color should match this selected "
"color."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/tools/enclose_and_fill.rst:50
msgid ".. image:: images/tools/enclose_and_fill_potential_areas.png"
msgstr ".. image:: images/tools/enclose_and_fill_potential_areas.png"

#: ../../reference_manual/tools/enclose_and_fill.rst:50
msgid ""
"An image illustrating the different areas that can be found by this tool "
"within this image. Each area has a different outline to indicate it's a "
"separate area. The following examples all show these outlines to demonstrate "
"which areas are selected, but note that they are for demonstration only and "
"would not show in a real situation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/tools/enclose_and_fill.rst:54
msgid ""
"When :guilabel:`Reference` is set to :guilabel:`All Layers` only areas of "
"the canvas that show the transparency checkers are considered transparent."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/tools/enclose_and_fill.rst:56
msgid ""
"All these options have a toggle for :guilabel:`invert`, which inverts which "
"regions are filled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/tools/enclose_and_fill.rst:60
msgid ".. image:: images/tools/enclose_and_fill_potential_areas_fill_all.png"
msgstr ".. image:: images/tools/enclose_and_fill_potential_areas_fill_all.png"

#: ../../reference_manual/tools/enclose_and_fill.rst:60
msgid ""
"Demonstration of which areas will be filled when using :guilabel:`All "
"Regions` and the given enclosing area. Blue areas are the selected areas."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/tools/enclose_and_fill.rst:63
msgid "All Regions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/tools/enclose_and_fill.rst:63
msgid "Any regions found will be filled. Most basic option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/tools/enclose_and_fill.rst:65
msgid ""
"The following options have an option for :guilabel:`Include Contour "
"Regions`, which will also fill everything that follows the chosen "
"conditions, but isn't completely enclosed by the enclosing area."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/tools/enclose_and_fill.rst:69
msgid ".. image:: images/tools/enclose_and_fill_potential_areas_fill_area.png"
msgstr ".. image:: images/tools/enclose_and_fill_potential_areas_fill_area.png"

#: ../../reference_manual/tools/enclose_and_fill.rst:69
msgid ""
"Topleft: :guilabel:`Regions of a Specific Color` set to cream white, "
"topright: :guilabel:`Transparent Regions`, bottom: :guilabel:`Regions of a "
"specific color or transparent`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/tools/enclose_and_fill.rst:71
msgid "Regions of a Specific Color."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/tools/enclose_and_fill.rst:72
msgid ""
"Only regions that are a specific color will be filled. If you have a complex "
"image where separate figures have their whole silhouette in a seperate "
"color, this can be used to only affect the silhouette of a single figure."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/tools/enclose_and_fill.rst:73
msgid "Transparent Regions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/tools/enclose_and_fill.rst:74
msgid ""
"Only regions that are transparent will be filled. Useful for filling a line "
"art."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/tools/enclose_and_fill.rst:76
msgid "Regions of a specific color or transparent."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/tools/enclose_and_fill.rst:76
msgid "Combines the transparent and specific color options."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/tools/enclose_and_fill.rst:80
msgid ""
".. image:: images/tools/enclose_and_fill_potential_areas_fill_all_except.png"
msgstr ""
".. image:: images/tools/enclose_and_fill_potential_areas_fill_all_except.png"

#: ../../reference_manual/tools/enclose_and_fill.rst:80
msgid ""
"Topleft: :guilabel:`All regions except those of a specific color` set to "
"cream white, topright: :guilabel:`All regions except transparent ones`, "
"bottomleft: :guilabel:`All regions except those of a specific color or "
"transparent`, and bottomright: :guilabel:`All regions except transparent "
"ones` with :guilabel:`Include Contour Regions` turned on, limited to a small "
"area."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/tools/enclose_and_fill.rst:82
msgid "All regions except those of a specific color."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/tools/enclose_and_fill.rst:83
msgid ""
"Fill all regions except ones with the selected color. If you set the "
"selected color to red and the :guilabel:`Threshold` to say, 50, then not "
"just red, but also colors close to red, like pink and orange will be avoided."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/tools/enclose_and_fill.rst:84
msgid "All regions except transparent ones."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/tools/enclose_and_fill.rst:85
msgid ""
"Fill all regions except transparent ones. This is useful when you've first "
"filled out a silhouette, so only select areas that are within that "
"silhouette."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/tools/enclose_and_fill.rst:87
msgid "All regions except those of a specific color or transparent."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/tools/enclose_and_fill.rst:87
msgid "Fill neither transparent nor the specific color."
msgstr ""

