msgstr ""
".. image:: images/tools/enclose_and_fill_potential_areas_fill_surrounded.png"

#: ../../reference_manual/tools/enclose_and_fill.rst:91
msgid ""
"Topleft: To demonstrate the following features the sample image got some "
"adjustments: The outlines were colored and some red silhouettes of "
"strawberries were added. Topright :guilabel:`Regions surrounded by a "
"specific color` set to grey, bottomleft: :guilabel:`Regions surrounded by "
"transparent`, and bottomright: :guilabel:`Regions surrounded by a specific "
"color or transparent`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/tools/enclose_and_fill.rst:93
msgid "Regions surrounded by a specific color."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/tools/enclose_and_fill.rst:94
msgid ""
"Fill all regions surrounded by a specific color. This is useful when you "
"have line art that uses different colored outlines for different features."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/tools/enclose_and_fill.rst:95
msgid "Regions surrounded by transparent."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/tools/enclose_and_fill.rst:96
msgid ""
"Fill regions that are surrounded by transparent. If you set the blending "
"mode to :guilabel:`Erase`, this can be used to clean up tiny dots and other "
"noise in a transparent area without affecting the main drawing."
msgstr ""

